{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103092","id":2347972812,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6L8zjM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103092","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103092.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103092.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103092","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103092/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103092/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103092/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8888f9e649a37d00b65996cbe8a56e42bee6647c","number":103092,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix uninitialized value in Tonemap","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"And anything that uses luminance.\r\n\r\nThe class Luminance in luminance.cpp is in charge of averaging the luminance of all pixels.\r\nIt performs multiple passes until it reaches a 1x1 texture containing the total average. This is standard luminance averaging on GPU.\r\n\r\nThen the \"result\" of this frame and the \"prev_frame_result\" are averaged together at a certain speed to mimic eye adaptation.\r\n\r\nThen this avarege becomes the \"source\" for the next frame. This is done here:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nSWAP(p_luminance_buffers->current,\r\np_luminance_buffers->reduce.write[p_luminance_buffers->reduce.size() -\r\n1]);\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo far pretty normal stuff.\r\n\r\n**The problem is: prev_frame_result IS UNINITIALIZED**. Therefore it's possible for prev_frame_result to contain garbage values like -5+e15 which causes the screen to stay black for a minute until eye adaptation catches up.\r\n\r\nWindows will always force allocations to be reset to 0, but Linux does not do that.\r\nHowever Windows just delays the bug; because it's possible for VMA to reuse a block.\r\n\r\nYou can repro this bug by downloading Bistro, creating a camera, selecting a default scene; and then launching Bistro.\r\n\r\nEverything will work fine.\r\nUntil you decide to resize the window. It takes a few tries on Godot, but eventually the screen becomes black.\r\n\r\nIf you wait around a minute, the screen will \"unblack\" itself back to normal.\r\n\r\nEven if it's not stuck in black after resize, you may notice that every resize is inconsistent in how the eye adaptation catches up (i.e. sometimes it flashes to white, sometimes it does not).\r\n\r\nIf you can't repro the bug, you need to try harder by doing arbitrary resizes until it triggers.\r\nAlso, I advise to try this on Linux; since Windows' sanitization of memory gets in the way.\r\n\r\nThere's probably multiple tickets already filled around issues that were rooted in luminance calculations starting from uninitialized memory.\r\n\r\nThis PR sets a default value of 0, which causes the screen to always flash white after resize. Setting a different value like 0.1 makes the flash effect weaker. Setting it to a high value like 5.0 makes the screen flash from dark instead.\r\n\r\nThis bug can be backported to 4.3. I don't know if it can be backported to earlier; as the render graph makes sure the texture_clear() calls gets issued in the right place; whereas in <= 4.2 it might be problematic depending on when Luminance::LuminanceBuffers::configure is being called.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7008779076,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABocF7RA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/cherrypick:4.3","name":"cherrypick:4.3","description":"Considered for cherry-picking into a future 4.3.x release","color":"446699","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMj